## 2. Surface Tint System

V2 replaces the single grey body background with **per-card surface gradients** using `color-mix()`. This creates a warm, layered depth without hard color blocks.

```css
/* Body — clean white canvas */
background: var(--brand-white);   /* NOT a grey wash */

/* Card surfaces — use the right surface for the right context */
--surface-impact:   linear-gradient(180deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-cloud-blue) 42%, white) 0%, white 72%);
/* → Impact / stat cards. Cool top-tint fades to white. */

--surface-action:   linear-gradient(168deg, white 0%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-cloud-blue) 28%, white) 100%);
/* → Default quick-action cards. White-led, subtle cloud-blue at bottom-right. */

--surface-cad-hub:  linear-gradient(128deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-cloud-blue) 55%, white) 0%, white 48%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-light-blue) 12%, white) 100%);
/* → Full-width UNERA CAD hub. Richest surface — signals a premium, compound module. */

--surface-warm:     linear-gradient(168deg, white 0%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-earth) 18%, white) 100%);
/* → Exchange/warm-action card. Earth tint = "value movement". */

--surface-sky:      linear-gradient(168deg, white 0%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-cloud-blue) 30%, white) 100%);
/* → Explore/info card. Lightest cool tint. */

--surface-deep:     linear-gradient(168deg, white 0%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-deep-blue) 7%, white) 100%);
/* → Wallet card. Faintest deep-blue whisper — implies value storage. */
```

**Rule**: Never use a flat hex for card backgrounds. Always reach for a `--surface-*` token or compose a new one with `color-mix()`.

