## 4. Navigation Color Scheme

V1 used a white nav. V2 uses a **dark ink gradient band** — a deliberate upgrade signal.

```css
.nav {
    background: var(--gradient-ink);   /* black → deep blue */
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
}

/* Link colors on dark background */
.nav-link          { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); }
.nav-link:hover    { color: var(--brand-yellow); }     /* Yellow on dark = active accent */
.nav-link.active   { color: var(--brand-yellow); font-weight: 600; }
.nav-link:focus    { outline: 2px solid var(--brand-yellow); }

/* User avatar */
.user-avatar-nav {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--brand-yellow) 0%, var(--brand-earth) 100%);
    color: var(--brand-deep-blue);   /* Yellow avatar = premium identity chip */
}

/* Notification badge */
.notif-badge {
    background: var(--brand-yellow);
    color: var(--brand-deep-blue);
    border: 2px solid var(--brand-deep-blue);   /* Dark border on dark nav = crisp ring */
}

/* Network indicator dot */
.network-indicator { background: var(--brand-yellow); }
```

**Rule**: On the dark nav — yellow (`--brand-yellow`) is the ONLY active/hover/accent color. Never use green or blue.

