## 5. Button Color System

Three tiers; each serves a distinct decision-weight:

```css
/* Primary CTA — Deep Blue fill, white text */
.btn-primary {
    background: var(--brand-deep-blue);
    color: var(--brand-white);
}
.btn-primary:hover {
    background: var(--neutral-800);   /* slightly lighter deep blue */
    box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(23, 61, 71, 0.35);
}

/* Multi-step / quote flows (Get CAD, Redeem CAD, similar): prefer --gradient-deep + white text — see §7.2 */

/* Secondary / outline */
.btn-secondary {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    border: 2px solid var(--border-subtle);
}
.btn-secondary:hover {
    border-color: var(--brand-deep-blue);
    color: var(--brand-deep-blue);
}

/* Alert CTA (on gradient-warm banner) — invert: Deep Blue fill, Yellow text */
.alert-cta {
    background: var(--brand-deep-blue);
    color: var(--brand-yellow);   /* Yellow text on deep blue = attention-grabbing, on-brand */
}

/* Primary action card (ink gradient background) */
.action-card.primary {
    background: var(--gradient-ink);   /* ties visually to nav */
    color: white;
    border: none;
}

/* Icon container inside the primary card — white chip, black icon */
/* Rationale: solid white reads as a "punched-out" premium chip against the ink gradient.
   The SVG stroke inherits black so the icon reads clearly on the white chip,
   matching the behaviour of all other action cards (dark icon on light chip).
   Never use rgba(255,255,255,0.25) — the frosted semi-transparent look is
   visually inconsistent with the solid-chip pattern used on secondary cards. */
.action-card.primary .action-card-icon {
    background: var(--brand-white);
}
.action-card.primary .action-card-icon svg {
    stroke: var(--brand-black);   /* explicit black — do NOT rely on color:inherit from the white parent */
}
```

**Focus rings**: Use `var(--brand-deep-blue)` on light surfaces, `var(--brand-yellow)` on dark/ink surfaces.

