## 6. Per-Card Icon Background Differentiation

Each icon container uses a unique subtle gradient so cards are instantly scannable without text:

```css
.impact-icon--portfolio { background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(23,61,71,0.20) 0%, rgba(106,87,112,0.18) 100%); }   /* deep+purple */
.impact-icon--yield     { background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(235,252,245,0.90) 0%, rgba(139,172,177,0.35) 100%); } /* cloud-blue */
.impact-icon--donations { background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(206,196,184,0.35) 0%, rgba(255,255,171,0.55) 100%); } /* earth+yellow */
.impact-icon--lives     { background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(23,61,71,0.18) 0%, rgba(139,172,177,0.30) 100%); }   /* deep+light-blue */
```

**Rule**: Never use a flat color for icon containers. Use angled gradients from the V2 brand palette at low opacity.

